    "summary": "A man&#039;s sash; long and red, with identical embroidery at each end.  Ground made of red tabby cotton cloth, commercially made. (One selvedge only; warp ends turned to front and hand stitched.)  Five registers of geometric embroidery [26.5 - 27.5 cms deep]: largest comprises motifs with diamond-shaped outline, with hooks.  Includes two lines with anthropomorphic motifs.  Worked in cross stitch embroidery using white, yellow, blue and green cotton yarns.  Unworn.",
